From f7d8add1c253850d2d55b77b9dcfd73af2138d64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: localhost-copilot <318096335+localhost-copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:32:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/meson: add fixed T7 OSD1 handoff alongside VDIN capture

Take over only the boot OSD1 address and VENC interrupt without running
global VPU, VPP, timing or TX initialization. Split VDIN resource claims
under an explicit profile while preserving its existing device paths.

Use atomic DRM objects and DMA GEM with a fixed RGB888 mode. Retire a
buffer only after two display interrupts and pin both references if the
latch times out. Keep this experiment built-in and reject suspend until
the complete display state has a lifecycle independent of firmware.

Signed-off-by: localhost-copilot <318096335+localhost-copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
